        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(commitments): avoid quadratic heartbeat session discovery",
        "body": "Related: #105787\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where heartbeat commitment fan-out loads and expires the commitments store under the queue/file lock, then scans the returned records once for every qualifying due record. When many due records belong to one session, that post-lock quadratic work increases heartbeat latency. Reported isolated medians were approximately 191 ms at 1,000 records, 847 ms at 2,000, and 2.28 s at 4,000.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe commitments store now builds the rolling 24-hour sent-count map once per agent and reuses it for due-session discovery and single-session due selection. The due-window, snooze, expiry, daily-cap, ordering, limit, agent-scope, queue, and cross-process file-lock behavior remain on the existing path.\n\nThis is intentionally an interim JSON-store fix. OpenClaw's shared SQLite state schema already contains a commitments table and indexes, but making it canonical requires a separate JSON-to-SQLite migration/doctor contract and broader persistence coverage. That migration remains a follow-up rather than expanding this focused latency fix.\n\n## User Impact\n\nHeartbeat commitment discovery changes from repeated full-store counting to one aggregation pass plus the existing due-record scan. Large concentrated sessions therefore scale linearly with store size instead of quadratically, without changing which sessions are eligible for delivery.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added a correctness test covering due-window filtering, snoozes, rolling daily caps, agent scope, and sorted session keys.\n- Added a concentrated-session scaling test with 8,000 due records in one session and one recent sent record. It uses the production-like `limit: 10`, so the base implementation scans all qualifying records and repeatedly rescans the store; the fixed implementation reuses one count map.\n- Added a runner-level proof using the production `startHeartbeatRunner` and `runHeartbeatOnce` path, a real temporary JSON state directory, 16,000 concentrated due records, and one recent sent record. The model/channel boundary is stubbed to keep the run secretless and deterministic; the scheduler, JSON load, due-session discovery, and fan-out path are real.\n- Reproducible focused commands:\n\n  ```sh\n  node scripts/run-vitest.mjs --config test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts src/commitments/store.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n  node scripts/run-vitest.mjs --config test/vitest/vitest.infra.config.ts src/infra/heartbeat-runner.commitments.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n  ```\n\n  Exact-head before/after proof, using the same local linked-worktree fallback and dependency cache because Crabbox was unavailable:\n\n  ```text\n  main 6c88469110 + proof test: REAL_HEARTBEAT_PROOF {\"commitmentCount\":16000,\"commitmentRunCount\":1,\"elapsedMs\":1267,\"globalRunStatus\":\"ran\",\"store\":\"json\"}; 14/14 tests passed\n  PR fcb249f495:       REAL_HEARTBEAT_PROOF {\"commitmentCount\":16000,\"commitmentRunCount\":1,\"elapsedMs\":507,\"globalRunStatus\":\"ran\",\"store\":\"json\"}; 14/14 tests passed\n  ```\n\n  Both runs exercised one global heartbeat and one commitment-only fan-out with a real JSON state directory. The local elapsed values are environment-sensitive; the durable scaling assertion is the 8,000-record store test above.\n\n  The fallback environment was:\n\n  ```sh\n  OPENCLAW_TEST_HEAVY_CHECK_LOCK_HELD=1 OPENCLAW_VITEST_FS_MODULE_CACHE_PATH=/tmp/openclaw-vitest-heartbeat-proof-cache-8 PNPM_CONFIG_MODULES_DIR=/root/openclaw/node_modules node scripts/run-vitest.mjs --config test/vitest/vitest.infra.config.ts src/infra/heartbeat-runner.commitments.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n  ```\n\n- Final focused store result: 11/11 tests passed; concentrated 8,000-record test body duration 272 ms.\n- `git diff --check`, `oxfmt --check`, and `oxlint` passed for the three changed files.\n- Fresh post-rebase branch autoreview against `origin/main`: `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode branch --base origin/main --engine codex --thinking high` — clean.\n- Crabbox was unavailable for remote execution because the configured client has no coordinator/broker authentication (`accessAuth: missing`, `brokerAuth: missing`); Blacksmith Testbox was likewise unauthenticated. Updated-head GitHub CI remains the remote validation gate.\n\n## AI-Assisted Disclosure\n\nThis PR was prepared with Codex and is AI-assisted. I reviewed the implementation, its callers, sibling selection path, persistence/locking behavior, tests, and the SQLite/Kysely storage contracts.\n",
